From 1c9648c4172bdaf43039b921bb04917a4fc79564 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 08:17:01 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 129/130] render: keep shader text work on disk across launches

Every load of a scene redid all of its shader text work, though a scene feeds it the same texts at every launch and
many times within one build (3042492564 builds 253 programs from 68 distinct shader pairs): each unit's WE text
passes (ShaderUnit::compile) and each pair's translation by glslang + SPIRV-Cross (GLSLContext::toGlsl). Of
3042492564's warm build (~1.0 s) they took ~0.33 s and ~0.44 s.

wp_config_set_shader_cache_dir names a directory where both keep their results: one file per result,
`<hash>.unit` / `<hash>.glsl`, named after an FNV-1a hash of its kind and key texts and holding the core's ELF build
id, the kind, every key and every value, LZ4-compressed. A `glsl` key is toGlsl's two input texts; a `unit` key is
everything compile reads (the unit's type and file, its preprocessed text and extensions, its override / pass /
discovered combos, and the linked unit's preprocessed text and combos). A hit needs the build id, the kind and
every key byte-equal, so another build of the core, a hash collision or a torn or corrupt file reads as a miss: the
work is done again and the file rewritten. Entries are written to a temporary file and renamed into place. The
build id stands for the code that turns keys into values (the text passes, glslang, SPIRV-Cross, their options);
the core now links with --build-id=sha1, since the Nix toolchain adds none, and a core without one caches nothing.
While the health report or a capture (the shader sweep) is on, reads are skipped: their records come from the work
itself. A failed translation is never stored. The unit's preprocessing (includes, uniforms, texture formats) still
runs at every load: it resolves textures and builds the pass's parameters. Unset, nothing changes.

Measured on a private headless liascape-player, apply to first frame (scene_load.py), 3042492564: warm 1240 ms
-> 528 ms (text passes 325 -> 102, translation 438 -> 7); first launch with empty caches 1596 -> 1132. 33 library
scenes, cache off vs on: warm build 17.8 s -> 10.8 s in all (median scene 187 -> 131 ms). Same output: the GL
text of every program (1720 in the 33 scenes) hashed identical in every load that finished, three per scene with
the cache off and three with it on. About 8 KB an entry; 3042492564's 206 entries take 1.6 MB.

Origin: ours
Why: docs/TODO.md (scene wallpapers load radically faster; the shader text work gets the same inputs at every launch)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01THaJ7t24KARpRjSyjTokdT
